cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the manuscript for mathematical results and this software version and commit for computations."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility software for a theoretical study of endogenous systemic
  market drawdown reachability under resilient liquidity, nonlinear price
  impact and paired-dollar execution in an idealized multi-asset market.
  Includes numerical checks, one interval-certified ten-asset existence
  construction and a partial Lean 4 formalization of foundational results.
keywords:
  - market crash reachability
  - endogenous market crashes
  - systemic drawdown
  - market microstructure
  - nonlinear price impact
  - market resilience
  - mathematical finance
  - interval arithmetic
  - Lean 4
title: "When Can Markets Crash Without News? — Reproducibility Software"
authors:
  - family-names: Ye
    given-names: Siyuan
